# beforeUpdate / updated

- `beforeUpdate` – called before the DOM is patched after a data change. You can read the current DOM state before updates.
- `updated` – called after the DOM has been re‑rendered. Avoid modifying state here to prevent infinite loops.

**Use cases**:
- Perform side effects after the DOM updates (e.g., scroll to a new position).
- Apply custom DOM manipulations based on new data.

```javascript
updated() {
  // log the new DOM height
  console.log(this.$el.scrollHeight);
}
```
